    "file": "published",
    "row_column": "clock_quality",
    "rows": {
      "published": 2191
    },
    "rule": "Each row's state and stated hours come from the circulars in evidence_ids, and available_utc is 00:00 UTC of the day after the latest of their issue dates: the annual trading-holiday circular alone for the dates it governs, plus the Revision in Trading Hours circular that states the evening close where one covers the date, plus any single-date circular such as an election closure, a Muhurat timing or a budget-day live session. Every row is published, so a default point-in-time read returns it from its available_utc on. The open and evening-only dates from 2026-11-02 to 2026-12-31 are published from the 2026 holiday circular alone, available from 2025-12-16, because no retained Revision in Trading Hours circular covers them. Their evening close is 23:55 with hours_notified false: the later of the two closes MCX has used since October 2020, a bound that is never earlier than the real close and not a time any circular states. A row is not revised once a release has carried it: an hours circular issued later applies only to dates added after 2026-12-31."
  },
  "columns": [
    {
      "meaning": "Asia/Kolkata civil date",
      "name": "session_date",
      "type": "date32[day]"
    },
    {
      "meaning": "three-letter weekday name",
      "name": "weekday",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "meaning": "open | morning_only | evening_only | closed",
      "name": "state",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "meaning": "start of the first trading window, IST; null when the morning session is shut",
      "name": "morning_open_ist",
      "type": "time64[us]"
    },
    {
      "meaning": "end of the first trading window, IST",
      "name": "morning_close_ist",
      "type": "time64[us]"
    },
    {
      "meaning": "start of the second trading window, IST; null when the evening session is shut",
      "name": "evening_open_ist",
      "type": "time64[us]"
    },
    {
      "meaning": "end of the second trading window, IST. Where a Revision in Trading Hours circular covers the date (hours_notified true) it is that circular's close: 23:30 while New York is on daylight time, 23:55 otherwise. Where none does (hours_notified false) it is 23:55, the later of the two, a bound that is never earlier than the real close and not a notified time. Muhurat and special windows carry their own times; null on closed dates and on an announced session no circular has timed",
      "name": "evening_close_ist",
      "type": "time64[us]"
    },
    {
      "meaning": "true when a retained Revision in Trading Hours circular covers this date. false when none does: on an open or evening-only date evening_close_ist is then the 23:55 bound and not a notified time; an announced session no circular has timed (the Muhurat of 2026-11-08) has null windows; on a closed date the flag only records whether a circular's period spans it",
      "name": "hours_notified",
      "type": "bool"
    },
    {
      "meaning": "muhurat | budget_live_session | delayed_open | null",
      "name": "special_session",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "meaning": "holiday as printed in the circular, null on ordinary days",
      "name": "holiday_name",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "meaning": "ids of the captured circulars that state something about this date (build/mcx/raw/circulars/<id>.pdf)",
      "name": "evidence_ids",
      "type": "list<item: string>"
    },
    {
      "meaning": "free text for anything non-standard",
      "name": "note",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "meaning": "00:00 UTC of the day after the latest issue date among this row's evidence_ids: the instant by which every circular the row relies on had been published. A bound close is not a circular and does not move it",
      "name": "available_utc",
      "type": "timestamp[us, tz=UTC]"
    },
    {
      "meaning": "published on every row: the state and the stated times are backed by the circulars in evidence_ids and available_utc is the instant they were all published. A close shown with hours_notified false is a bound, not a stated time. Pack v2.0.1 classed 43 rows unvintaged; none is",
      "name": "clock_quality",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
  "date_range": {
    "end": "2026-12-31",
    "start": "2021-01-01",
    "states": {
      "closed": 645,
      "evening_only": 67,
      "morning_only": 7,
      "open": 1472
    }
  },
  "name": "mcx_sessions",
  "notes": [
    "Hours are for internationally referenceable non-agricultural commodities (gold, silver, copper, crude oil); agricultural contracts close earlier.",
    "Weekend dates are closed unless a circular states a session (budget-day live sessions, Sunday Muhurat trading).",
    "Muhurat and budget-day sessions are stored with their own trading windows in the open/close columns and flagged in special_session; the state column keeps the four-value enum.",
    "No retained circular states the evening close from 2026-11-01. The open and evening-only dates from 2026-11-02 to 2026-12-31 carry 23:55 with hours_notified=false: the later of 23:30 and 23:55, an upper bound, so no instant inside the real session falls after it. The feed's mcx_calendar.py trades the shorter 23:30 on the same dates, the cautious choice for a desk. The Revision in Trading Hours circular for the US clock change of 2026-11-01 is not among the retained circulars.",
    "The 2026-11-08 Muhurat session is announced by the 2026 holiday circular, which says its timings 'shall be notified subsequently'. Its row has no times; the instant used to date its Bhav Copy is 23:55 IST, never earlier than the real close.",
    "The table ends 2026-12-31 because the 2027 Trading Holidays circular is not among the retained circulars. MCX issued the circulars for 2021 to 2026 on 2020-12-11, 2021-12-10, 2022-12-09, 2023-12-14, 2024-12-13 and 2025-12-15. Dates of 2027 are added as new rows when it is retained; no row of this table changes then.",
    "2026 differs from feed mcx_calendar.py on two circular-backed dates: 2026-01-15 (evening only, MCX/TRD/017/2026) and Sunday 2026-02-01 (special live session, MCX/TRD/027/2026)."
  ],
